From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EvilMetaMonkey <hood.mj85@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:05:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Splash: a symmetrical car, DMC <version>, the real host name

Every splash row is now a mirror image of itself (tested with / and \,
[ and ], ( and ) swapped). The header drops the carmaker's name, the
status row shows this machine's host name (shortened) instead of a fixed
one, and no film or carmaker names remain.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 CHANGELOG.md      |  1 +
 lib/src/ui.dart   | 56 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------------------
 test/ui_test.dart | 52 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 3 files changed, 66 insertions(+), 43 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 159ebcdbcd076a88324dae10a7b2cfd4ff325801..a7458a5688c5a8793580e36a18c528b636678314 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 ## Unreleased — Meta AI Developer Hackathon 2026
 
+- The splash car is symmetrical (every row a mirror image, tested), the header is `DMC <version>`, and the status row names this machine (its host name, shortened) instead of a fixed name. No film or carmaker names remain.
 - Add `dmc disable [--apply] [--json --schema-version 1]`. It removes only dmc's own agent hooks from every config file the installer supports (the workspace's project and local files and the user files), for this dmc build and others, through the exact-match uninstall with byte-exact restore, and stops the watcher. `.dmc/`, every checkpoint and other tools' hooks are untouched. Preview by default; re-enable with `dmc hooks install`.
 - `dmc doctor` checks agent hooks: a dmc executable that is missing or not executable, a hook pointing at a different dmc build, a Muse Code Interrupt hook that is not async, and an agent checkpoint left open longer than `--stale-hours` (default 2) by a session that looks ended. It suggests the fix and changes nothing.
 - `dmc hooks status` takes `--json --schema-version 1`. `capabilities` lists `hooks.status` and `disable` (features `hooksStatusJson`, `disable`), additively.
